From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: warelik <warelik@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:03:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] Add agent.threads_sidebar.in_agent_panel setting

Few people juggle as many threads as the threads sidebar holds, yet
keeping them in view costs a whole column, and toggling the sidebar
costs an action every time. With agent.threads_sidebar.in_agent_panel
the sidebar is not shown; its contents become two tab rows at the top
of the agent panel instead of the active thread's title: the window's
projects, then the threads and terminals of the active project. The
rows use the editor's tab component and follow the same tab settings
(pinned/unpinned chips, width bounds, close button position and
visibility), so they look and behave like the editor's two tab rows:
click activates, double-click renames, middle-click and the close
button archive a thread or close a terminal, right-click opens the
sidebar's menu for the project or thread. Thread tabs keep the order
they were opened in rather than the sidebar's most-recent-first order.

The sidebar entity stays the single model; the agent panel only gets
views of it through the SidebarHandle, since agent_ui cannot depend
on the sidebar crate. Thread history opens from the agent panel's menu
and replaces the thread until a tab is clicked or the history is
closed. Add Project sits at the end of the projects row. Toggling the
threads sidebar toggles the agent panel in this mode.

The setting defaults to false, which keeps the sidebar.

Drafts are preserved during pending activation when in_agent_panel is true
and strictly follow stock behavior when false. Tab order is deterministic
and preserved across thread updates using stable created_at timestamps.
Traffic light layout in the panel header is gated for macOS, allowing
compilation on Linux and Windows. Stale sidebar_open checks are replaced
with active render state checks. Settings deserialization safely defaults
in_agent_panel to false with regression unit tests.
